<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP 9-mth oil/condensate output up.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP 9-mth oil/condensate output up.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Tuesday oil and condensate production rose two percent in the nine months to February, while gas production fell five percent.  </p>
<p>BHP said oil and condensate production was stable during February at 5.267 million barrels, but rose two percent on a year-to-date basis to 50.944 million barrels.</p>
<p>Higher production in Europe, mainly due to commencement of Liverpool Bay, was offset by lower production from Australia/Asia and the Americas Region.</p>
<p>Production during February at Griffin and Wanaea/Cossack was hit by weather and downtime for repair work, while the Skua field in the Timor Sea was shut-in at the end of January after it reached the end of its commercial life.  </p>
<p>Gas production fell 11 percent in February to 17.7 billion cubic feet and five percent on a year to date basis to 187.5 billion cubic feet.</p>
<p>The decrease was due mainly to the sale of onshore North American gas assets, BHP said.</p>
<p>The commissioning of the Hamilton gas field in the Liverpool Bay development during January and the first half of February also led to oil and gas production being shut in for part of the month, it said.</p>
